# pull-sources.conf — sources for ver-pull-session.sh (installed at
# /etc/nwp-server/pull-sources.conf on `ver`). One source per line:
#
#   name|from_repo|to_repo|kind
#
# Fields:
#   name      keystore-entry stem; `<name>.from` holds the source repo password.
#   from_repo prod's restic repo, reached over the 1:1 WireGuard tunnel, e.g.
#             sftp:<backup-user>@10.66.<N>.1:/var/backups/nwp-server/<site>
#   to_repo   ver's durable repo, e.g. /srv/ver-backups/<site>
#   kind      DATA CLASS (mandatory — the session fails closed without it):
#               raw        unsanitised user data (PII, NWP-ADR-0025). Gets a HARD
#                          30-day erasure ceiling (ver-backup-pull --keep-within
#                          30d) so no RAW snapshot outlives the erasure promise
#                          (ops#127/#124). Override the window with raw:<DUR>,
#                          e.g. raw:14d.
#               sanitized  no PII — keeps the tiered daily/weekly/monthly policy.
#
# Lines beginning with # and blank lines are ignored. Validate without going
# online:  ver-pull-session.sh --check
#
# Examples (replace with real repos; do NOT commit real hostnames):
# site1|sftp:backup@10.66.1.1:/var/backups/nwp-server/site1|/srv/ver-backups/site1|raw
# site2-pub|sftp:backup@10.66.1.1:/var/backups/nwp-server/site2-sanitized|/srv/ver-backups/site2-pub|sanitized
